The input needs an associated `<label>`; its placeholder disappears as users type. “Optional” at `#aaa` on white has insufficient contrast.

```html
<div class="note-field">
  <label for="internal-note">Internal note</label>
  <p id="note-help">Optional</p>
  <input id="internal-note" type="text"
         aria-describedby="note-help" placeholder="Type a note">
  <button type="button">Save</button>
</div>
```

```css
.note-field { background: #fff; color: #222; }
.note-field label { display: block; font-weight: 600; }
.note-field p { color: #595959; margin: .25rem 0 .5rem; }
.note-field input { display: block; margin-bottom: .75rem; }
.note-field input:focus-visible,
.note-field button:focus-visible {
  outline: 3px solid #1a73e8;
  outline-offset: 2px;
}
```
